---
import measurements from '../content/kundt-measurements.json';
import regression from '../content/kundt-regression.json';

interface Props {
  paragraphs: string[];
}

const { paragraphs } = Astro.props;
const [apparatus, spacing, powder] = paragraphs;
const assetUrl = (path: string) => `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}${path}`;
---

<div class="kundt-experiment">
  <section class="experiment-stage" aria-labelledby="kundt-demonstration-title">
    <h4 id="kundt-demonstration-title">Demonstration</h4>
    <p>The video shows mode 2. The beads rise in two distinct regions, marking the two displacement antinodes. At the displacement node in the centre, the beads remain still.</p>
    <figure class="video-reservation" data-kundt-stage="demonstration">
      <div class="video-space">
        <video controls playsinline preload="metadata" poster={assetUrl('media/scienteens/kundt-demonstration-poster.webp')} aria-label="Kundt tube demonstration with beads">
          <source src={assetUrl('media/scienteens/kundt-demonstration.mp4')} type="video/mp4" />
          Your browser does not support embedded video.
        </video>
      </div>
      <figcaption>Mode 2: two antinodes where the beads rise, separated by a central node where they remain still.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="experiment-stage" aria-labelledby="kundt-measurement-title">
    <h4 id="kundt-measurement-title">Measurement</h4>
    <p>{apparatus}</p>
    <p>{spacing}</p>
    <p>{powder}</p>
    <p>We used a {measurements.tubeLengthM.toFixed(2)} m tube closed at both ends, with air at {measurements.airTemperatureC.toFixed(1)} °C. The frequencies for modes 2 to 5 were taken from the calculated modes of this tube, using a reference speed of {measurements.referenceSpeedMS.toFixed(0)} m/s.</p>
    <p>For each mode, we measured the distances between neighbouring nodes and took their mean, d. The wavelength is twice this mean: λ = 2d. For mode 2, the measured spacing of {measurements.readings[0].meanNodeSpacingCm.toFixed(1)} cm therefore gives a wavelength of {(2 * measurements.readings[0].meanNodeSpacingCm / 100).toFixed(3)} m.</p>
    <figure class="video-reservation" data-kundt-stage="measurement">
      <div class="video-space">
        <video controls playsinline preload="metadata" poster={assetUrl('media/scienteens/kundt-measurement-poster.webp')} aria-label="Kundt tube node-spacing measurement, modes 2 to 5">
          <source src={assetUrl('media/scienteens/kundt-measurement.mp4')} type="video/mp4" />
          Your browser does not support embedded video.
        </video>
      </div>
      <figcaption>Identify neighbouring nodes, measure their separations and compare the mean distances for modes 2, 3, 4 and 5.</figcaption>
    </figure>

  </section>

  <section class="experiment-stage" aria-labelledby="kundt-results-title">
    <h4 id="kundt-results-title">Results</h4>
    <figure class="measurement-graph" data-kundt-stage="graph">
      <picture>
        <source media="(max-width: 38rem)" srcset={assetUrl('media/scienteens/kundt-sound-speed-mobile.svg')} width="440" height="550" />
        <img
          src={assetUrl('media/scienteens/kundt-sound-speed.svg')}
          alt={`Driving frequency in hertz plotted against inverse measured wavelength in reciprocal metres for modes 2 to 5. A linear fit through the origin gives a speed of ${regression.speedMS.toFixed(2)} metres per second and R squared of ${regression.rSquared.toFixed(6)}. Air temperature: ${measurements.airTemperatureC.toFixed(1)} degrees Celsius.`}
          width="900"
          height="550"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </picture>
      <figcaption>
        <strong>Driving frequency as a function of inverse wavelength</strong>
        <span>Each point represents one mode. The dashed line is the linear regression through the origin; its slope gives the speed of sound.</span>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <table>
      <caption>Selected frequencies and measured mean spacings, at {measurements.airTemperatureC.toFixed(1)} °C. Wavelengths are calculated using λ = 2d.</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Mode n</th>
          <th scope="col">f (Hz)</th>
          <th scope="col">Mean d (cm)</th>
          <th scope="col">λ (m)</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {measurements.readings.map((reading) => (
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">{reading.mode}</th>
            <td>{reading.frequencyHz.toFixed(1)}</td>
            <td>{reading.meanNodeSpacingCm.toFixed(1)}</td>
            <td>{(2 * reading.meanNodeSpacingCm / 100).toFixed(3)}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <p>As the frequency increases, the measured wavelength decreases. We plot the frequency f against 1/λ. Since f = v × (1/λ), the slope of this graph gives the speed of sound. The regression uses all four points and passes through the origin.</p>
    <p>The slope gives <strong>v = {regression.speedMS.toFixed(2)} m/s</strong>. The four points lie very close to the fitted line (R² = {regression.rSquared.toFixed(6)}), so the measurements are consistent with the same speed of sound for all four frequencies.</p>
  </section>
</div>

<style>
  .kundt-experiment { min-width: 0; }
  .experiment-stage { margin-top: var(--space-5); }
  h4 { margin: 0 0 var(--space-3); font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.55rem; letter-spacing: -0.035em; line-height: 1.1; }
  p { color: var(--color-muted); font-size: 1.05rem; text-align: justify; hyphens: auto; }
  .video-reservation { max-width: var(--text-width); margin: var(--space-4) auto var(--space-5); }
  .video-space { aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid var(--color-line); border-radius: var(--radius-md); background: var(--color-bg); }
  .video-space video { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: contain; }
  figcaption { display: grid; gap: var(--space-1); padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-1) 0; color: var(--color-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  figcaption strong { color: var(--color-ink); font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1rem; }
  .measurement-graph { margin: var(--space-5) 0; }
  .measurement-graph img { width: 100%; height: auto; }
  table { width: 100%; margin: var(--space-4) 0; border-collapse: collapse; color: var(--color-ink); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  caption { padding-bottom: var(--space-3); color: var(--color-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; text-align: left; }
  th, td { padding: var(--space-2); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line); text-align: right; }
  thead th { color: var(--color-primary-dark); background: var(--color-surface-strong); }
  th:first-child { text-align: left; }
  @media (max-width: 38rem) {
    table { font-size: 0.88rem; }
    th, td { padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-1); }
  }
</style>
